          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy-900">Application fees or fee waivers</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
              Budget roughly $130 per school in fees and CAS reports, and apply for LSAC and
              school-level fee waivers early if you are eligible.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-white p-5">
          <span class="flex h-7 w-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-navy-900 text-xs font-semibold text-white">8</span>
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy-900">Interview prep (where offered)</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
              Northwestern interviews nearly everyone; several other schools offer optional
              interviews. Prepare a clear "why law" and "why this school" answer.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Competitor comparison -->
  <section id="comparison" class="section-pad scroll-mt-24 border-t border-[var(--line)]">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <h2 class="text-balance text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-navy-950">
        How We Compare to 7Sage, LSD.law, and LSAC
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-[65ch] text-[var(--muted)]">
        Several tools promise to estimate your law school chances. Here is an honest, side-by-side
        look at what each one actually offers.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-white">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[720px] border-collapse text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--soft)] text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-navy-900">Feature</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-navy-900">This Site</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-navy-900">7Sage</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-navy-900">LSD.law</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-navy-900">LSAC</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {COMPARISON_ROWS.map((row) => (
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--line)] last:border-0">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-navy-900">{row.feature}</td>
                <td class={`px-4 py-3 ${row.oursAdvantage ? 'bg-navy-50 font-medium text-navy-900' : 'text-[var(--muted)]'}`}>
                  {row.ours}
                </td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-[var(--muted)]">{row.sevenSage}</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-[var(--muted)]">{row.lsd}</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-[var(--muted)]">{row.lsac}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {Object.values(COMPETITORS).map((c) => (
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-white p-6">
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold tracking-tight text-navy-900">
              <a href={c.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="hover:underline">{c.name}</a>
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">{c.description}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section id="faq" class="section-pad scroll-mt-24 border-t border-[var(--line)]">
    <div class="page-shell max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-balance text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-navy-950">
        Frequently Asked Questions
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-4">
        {faqs.map((f) => (
          <details class="group rounded-xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-white">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-navy-900">
              {f.q}
              <svg
                class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-[var(--muted)] transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
              {f.a}
            </div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Data source & trust -->
  <section id="about-data" class="section-pad scroll-mt-24 border-t border-[var(--line)]">
    <div class="page-shell max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-balance text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-navy-950">
        About This Data
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-8 flex justify-center">
        <img
          src="/scales-of-justice.webp"
          alt="An antique brass scales of justice, symbolizing the transparent and balanced admissions model"
          width="800"
          height="800"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          class="h-auto w-56 rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] object-cover"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-4">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-white p-6">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-navy-900">Data source</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
            Every number on this page comes from{' '}
            <a
              href="https://www.americanbar.org/groups/legal_education/resources/statistics/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
              class="text-navy-800 underline decoration-navy-200 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-navy-800"
            >
              ABA 509 Required Disclosures
            </a>{' '}
            for the {DATA_YEAR} entering class — the standardized report every ABA-accredited law
            school must file annually. These are the same LSAT and GPA percentiles and acceptance
            rates that feed the U.S. News rankings, which is why they are the most reliable public
            admissions data available.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-[var(--muted)]">
            Data last updated: {DATA_YEAR} entering class
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-white p-6">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-navy-900">Methodology</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
            This calculator uses a transparent, median-based model — no black box. It measures how
            far your LSAT (weighted 60%) and GPA (weighted 40%) sit from each school's
            enrolled-student median and maps that distance to a probability. You can see exactly
            why a school is a reach or a safety, unlike machine-learning predictors that hide
            their reasoning.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-white p-6">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-navy-900">Limitations</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
            No calculator can see the parts of your application that admissions offices also weigh
            — essays, recommendations, work experience, and timing. Treat each percentage as a
            rough estimate, not a promise, and use the results to build a balanced list rather
            than to rule schools in or out. Medians rise slightly most years, so a score at last
            year's median may sit just below this year's.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
